<Doc>
    <p>In abide it is the handler, and a page that reads it. You declare what a value <em>is</em>,
    and reading it loads it — there is nothing in between for you to write.</p>

    <Section title="Call a server function from a page">
        <Example
            id="read-invoice"
            title="Read an invoice"
            summary="A row from your database on the page, with nothing between them. One file: the handler you would have written anyway, and the markup that reads it."
            files={{ 'Invoice.abide': invoiceSource }}
        >
            <Invoice />
        </Example>

        <p><em>1 file, 0 API in it</em> — one of those seven is left standing, and it is the
        handler. Its <code>&lt;script server&gt;</code> never reaches the browser; the page calls
        <code>getInvoice</code> by the name it was declared with.</p>
    </Section>

